    "body": "Review findings addressed in b8f1bad (quick gate green): speed - a 40-hole pecked radial program ~9.5 s -> ~0.25 s in debug (cylinders built once with bboxes, swept-box pre-filter newest first, stock bbox reject, one test for a disc inside a drilled hole, no duplicate samples), body step tightened to 0.5 mm, a wall-time test pins it; deterministic app test drilling_cross_rapids (a spliced hop through the bar is named and the post refuses - and the old box-stock test passed for the wrong reason, now fixed with a B-trunnion mill-turn); edge tests (past a drilled bottom, graze in/out of tolerance, half-in-hole retract); fails closed on non-finite context, unusable tool radius, directionless axis; zero flute = one diameter of body; drilling_cross.rs 565 -> 252 lines.",
